    "name": "tuning",
    "notes": "The one engine-tuning capture for this truck (2026-09-21). It replaces eight research profiles, each built to answer one question, whose answers are now in: fuel-target-research, fuel-pw-research, fuel-pw-research-2, injector-deadtime-idle, afr-delay-research, tuning-hybrid-research, fuel-did-research and rom-trace. Their definitions are kept verbatim in capture_profiles.archive.yaml, which nothing loads. Every capture also keeps its profile snapshot in its own manifest.\n\nBase: fuel-target-research, the configuration that ran cleanly on the 2026-09-21 drive (data/analyses/2026-09-21-drive-fuel-target-research.md). Changes from it:\n- Adds STFT and LTFT for both banks at 2 Hz. Their absence on that drive left closed-loop health unassessable.\n- Adds bank-2 A/F voltage and injected pulse 0x1206/0x1207. 0x1206 passed as the injected-pulse instrument on 2026-09-18.\n- Drops DID 0x1134. It is not commanded phi, and the commanded target is now read directly from RAM (mem:ECM_TARGET_EQUIV_RATIO).\n\nMemory windows: fuel_target (commanded phi and engine period) and spark (ignition timing and engine speed). Each window is a single service-0x23 read, so the two values in it come from the same instant.\n\nNot included: rom-trace's map-cell trace channels. That profile's continuous session stalled on 2026-09-21 with zero requests sent, and the cause is not known yet. The trace channels come back once it is found.\n\nMode 01 and Mode 22 alternate on this ECM, so each DID is read once per 0.5 s cycle, which gives 2 Hz.",
